## Refinements

1. **One mint site, not two.** `freshId` is also used by `mkElement` (`:815`, the
   static test scene at `:956-958`). The provider's `system` member must become the
   only `Guid.NewGuid` for element ids and `freshId` be deleted (reuse, never copy);
   `addElement` reads `model.elementIds`, `mkElement` uses `ElementIdProvider.system`.
2. **Keep it in the one authorized file.** Declare `ElementIdProvider` (record with
   `mintElementId : unit -> Library.ElementId`, `[<ReferenceEquality>]`, `system`
   member) in `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` rather than splitting it into Domain
   as `ItemIdProvider` is; it is the table's concern and the ruling stays one file
   wide. Name check: `ElementIdProvider`, `elementIds` and `mintElementId` must be
   free under ELEV014-016 (the elevation gate proves it).
3. **Verification.** The fixture must fail on exhaustion and assert full
   consumption (three ids), like its item ids. The reference kit must be regenerated
   from a build with the fix (the 116 untracked files now in `data/optics-mueller/`
   come from a random build and are stale in exactly the three ids), then the fact
   re-run on a second, independent build. Only the 26 gates of `.slices/0428.gates`
   as declared; I do not recommend the post-mortem's supplemental
   TableAndElementRotationTests/ElementMenuTests runs, which are outside the roster
   (the ui-smoke gate already exercises the default add path).

